{"records":[{"id":"9y8wvf53c8","title":"Supplementary Appendix - Differentiation of Keratoacanthoma and Well-Differentiated Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma Using Single-cell Spatial Pathology ","description":"Supplementary Appendix - Differentiation of Keratoacanthoma and Well-Differentiated Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma Using Single-cell Spatial Pathology ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-11-08T08:00:23.258Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9y8wvf53c8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9y8wvf53c8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jesse","last_name":"Veenstra","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Skin Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nvkxvz59bn","title":"Dissecting the immunosuppressive microenvironment via interaction of LAMC2+ basal cells and SPP1+ macrophages in invasive tumor front integrating spatial and single-cell transcriptomics in lung squamous cell carcinoma","description":"Data associated with manuscript \"Dissecting the immunosuppressive microenvironment via interaction of LAMC2+ basal cells and SPP1+ macrophages in invasive tumor front integrating spatial and single-cell transcriptomics in lung squamous cell carcinoma\" including single-cell data and spatial transcriptome data.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T09:10:14.879Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nvkxvz59bn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nvkxvz59bn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shengqiang","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Single-Cell RNA Sequencing","Spatial Transcriptomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zg488kvchw","title":"Untargeted Salivary Metabolomic Profiling Uncovers Metabolic Dysregulation in Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma Patients","description":"Raw mass spectrometry data of saliva samples from human subjects across three groups - healthy controls, oral potentially malignant disorders (OPMD), and oral squamous cell carcinoma (OSCC). Untargeted metabolomic profiling was carried out by liquid chromatography-high-resolution mass spectrometry (LC-HRMS) on Agilent 6545 Q-TOF for the manuscript entitled \"Untargeted Salivary Metabolomic Profiling Uncovers Metabolic Dysregulation in Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma Patients”. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-18T10:44:14.878Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zg488kvchw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zg488kvchw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Akanksha","last_name":"Bhattacharya","orcid":"0009-0003-1771-9732"},{"first_name":"Maynak","last_name":"Pal","orcid":"0000-0001-9467-517X"},{"first_name":"Ganakalyan","last_name":"Behera","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Deepti","last_name":"Joshi","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Anshul ","last_name":"Rai","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ashok","last_name":"Kumar","orcid":"0000-0001-7208-2947"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metabolomics","Oral Cancer","Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jkj7x7pjkg","title":"Low Prevalence of High-Risk Human Papillomavirus in Nail Unit Squamous Cell Carcinoma in Koreans using Next-generation Sequencing","description":"Supplementary materials of the article: \"Low Prevalence of High-Risk Human Papillomavirus in Nail Unit Squamous Cell Carcinoma in Koreans using Next-generation Sequencing\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-15T12:55:48.371Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jkj7x7pjkg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jkj7x7pjkg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Je-Ho","last_name":"Mun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Virus","Skin"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tc93htv96w","title":"Diagnosis and Management of Nail Unit Squamous Cell Carcinoma: A Clinical Review by an Expert Panel","description":"Curtis KL, Amin SP, Jellinek NJ, Knackstedt TJ, Miller CJ, Piraccini BM, Richert B, Rubin AI, Trakatelli MG, Lipner SR, Diagnosis and Management of Nail Unit Squamous Cell Carcinoma: A Clinical Review by an Expert Panel, JAAD Reviews (2025), doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdrv.2024.12.012.\n\nSupplemental Figure 1. Longitudinal reddish-brown band with very discrete hyperkeratosis of the lateral sulcus of the nail unit in a young male. His partner had conization for cervical dysplasia with human papillomavirus infection, a procedure in which part of the cervix is removed due to cervical dysplasia. Mohs micrographic surgery confirmed a superficial epidermoid carcinoma. The tumor was positive for HPV 56, supporting genital-digital transmission.\n\nSupplemental Figure 2. Nail unit squamous cell carcinoma management algorithm.\n\nSupplemental Table 1. Differential diagnosis for nail unit squamous cell carcinoma.\n\nSupplemental Table 2. Distinguishing features of nail unit squamous cell carcinoma vs. nail unit keratoacanthoma.\n\nSupplemental Table References.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-20T16:41:58.153Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tc93htv96w","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tc93htv96w"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kaya","last_name":"Curtis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Snehal","last_name":"Amin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathaniel","last_name":"Jellinek","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Knackstedt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christopher","last_name":"Miller","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bianca Maria","last_name":"Piraccini","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bertrand","last_name":"Richert","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Adam","last_name":"Rubin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Myrto","last_name":"Trakatelli","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Shari","last_name":"Lipner","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology","Nail Abnormality"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"88fcgj65bf","title":"Association of Human Papillomavirus and Extra-genital Bowen’s Disease (Squamous Cell Carcinoma in situ): A Systematic Review","description":"Supplementary materials for publication JAAD-D-20-02223 (Namgoong et al. Association of Human Papillomavirus and Extra-genital Bowen’s Disease (Squamous Cell Carcinoma in situ): A Systematic Review)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-20T13:19:57.542Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/88fcgj65bf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/88fcgj65bf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sik","last_name":"Namgoong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jaeyoung","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kyung Muk","last_name":"Jeong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiehyun","last_name":"Jeon","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hae Jun","last_name":"Song","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yoo Sang","last_name":"Baek","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wsgjv6sgrj","title":"Underrepresentation of Black Individuals in Basal Cell and Squamous Cell Carcinoma Clinical Trials: A Comparison to an Insurance Claimant Cohort","description":"This repository includes the statistical methods and analysis along with the data extracted from the included basal cell carcinoma and cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma clinical trials.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-03T13:56:37.69Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wsgjv6sgrj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wsgjv6sgrj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mara","last_name":"Hartoyo","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2bh5fchcv6","title":"Human squamous cell carcinoma, Visium","description":"Visium experiments on a squamous cell carcinoma from a human donor. Four serial 10 µm sections spaced 150 µm apart. Processed sequencing data from 10X Genomics Space Ranger version 1.0.0.\n\nA skin biopsy was collected from a patient with suspected squamous cell carcinoma after obtaining informed consent. The diagnosis was histologically verified by a board-certified dermatopathologist. The study protocol was approved by the Institutional Review Board at Stanford University Medical Center (protocol #21750).","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-08-20T18:32:59.091Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2bh5fchcv6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2bh5fchcv6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xesús","last_name":"Abalo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kim","last_name":"Thrane","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Andrew Lin","last_name":"Ji","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Reza","last_name":"Mirzazadeh","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Paul","last_name":"Khavari","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Joakim","last_name":"Lundeberg","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Transcriptomics","Squamous Cell Carcinoma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ngd9x6g9c5","title":"CSCC metastasis protein predictors","description":"Protein predictors of poor outcomes in cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma. Tables including cell counts and tests used to perform hypothesis testing. STATA file includes dataset for meta-analysis. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-08-21T19:33:35.593Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ngd9x6g9c5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ngd9x6g9c5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Patrick","last_name":"Mulvaney","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Medicine"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"dmt2p5jrnw","title":"Part I